<title>GERMANY: IG Metall attorney steps down over fee debate.</title>
<headline>IG Metall attorney steps down over fee debate.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael Kittner, legal advisor to German engineering union IG Metall, stepped down from his post after angering union board members for failing to inform them fully about an expensive consulting project.</p>
<p>IG Metall said in a statement, released on Monday, that Kittner's departure was linked to a 1.34 million mark honorarium the union paid to Horst Henrichs, president of the Frankfurt appellate court, for leading an internal investigation at the union.</p>
<p>While Kittner informed the board that Henrichs would do some consulting work he failed to tell the board how large the sum would be.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
